      <projectDesc>
        <p>Transcoded from a MusicXML version 2.0 file on<date>2012-07-06</date>using an XSLT stylesheet (musicxml2mei v. 2.2.3).</p>
        <p>Teaching derivative prepared 2026-10-24. Remove all body slurs, dynamics, tempo, verbal directions and articulation elements deliberately. Correct d1e338 and d1e1495 from A3 to F3 against the print. Keep the other notes, written durations, rests, voices, chords, accidentals, clefs, beams, stems and IDs. Whole piece retained; the core exercise concerns MEI labels 1–9 (pickup plus eight full bars). This file is not a complete edition of that passage.</p>
        <p>Base encoding: Maja Hartwig, MEI Sample Collection, commit e4a3c4dece588ae0bdb13e5cf956340dcd99b447. Upstream credits, rights statements, bibliography and revision history are retained. The duplicate header incipit is omitted. The witness controls new readings; the encoding is a starting document, not that witness. Instructor review is still required; no whole-piece editorial approval is asserted.</p>
        <p>Source-based pitch correction, 24 October 2026: the final bass eighth in MEI labels 2 and 6 reads F3 in IMSLP 51556, printed p. 8, systems 1 and 2. The reused encoding reads A3 (d1e338, d1e1495). Teaching notes/solutions use F3; the upstream original and technical baseline retain A3. Manual-entry placeholders contain no pitches. Further source review remains necessary.</p>
      </projectDesc>
      <samplingDecl>
        <p>encoding contains @accid.ges</p>
      </samplingDecl>
